IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `au-part4-repeal`

-- Tests for Part 4. Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Section 7(1): no revival unless express provision`

#ASSERT NOT (`the repeal of the repealing Act or part revives the old Act or part` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the repeal of the repealing Act or part revives the old Act or part` TRUE

§ `Section 7(2): what a repeal or amendment does not affect`

-- (a) revive anything not in force or existing.
#ASSERT `what a repeal or amendment does to` `something not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect` FALSE EQUALS `it is not revived`
-- (b) previous operation, anything duly done or suffered.
#ASSERT `what a repeal or amendment does to` `the previous operation of the affected Act or part, or anything duly done or suffered under it` FALSE EQUALS `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
-- (c) rights, privileges, obligations or liabilities acquired, accrued or incurred.
#ASSERT `what a repeal or amendment does to` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE EQUALS `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
-- (d) penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence committed against it.
#ASSERT `what a repeal or amendment does to` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against it` FALSE EQUALS `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
-- (e) investigation, legal proceeding or remedy.
#ASSERT `what a repeal or amendment does to` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment` FALSE EQUALS `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
-- A contrary intention (s 2(2)) displaces the rule for every kind of thing.
#ASSERT `what a repeal or amendment does to` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` TRUE EQUALS `section 7(2) gives no answer because a contrary intention appears`
#ASSERT `what a repeal or amendment does to` `something not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect` TRUE EQUALS `section 7(2) gives no answer because a contrary intention appears`

§ `Section 7(3): the five ways`

#ASSERT `counts as a repeal or amendment for section 7` `an express repeal or amendment`
#ASSERT `counts as a repeal or amendment for section 7` `a repeal or amendment effected by implication`
#ASSERT `counts as a repeal or amendment for section 7` `the expiry, lapsing or cessation of effect of the Act or part`
#ASSERT `counts as a repeal or amendment for section 7` `the abrogation or limitation of the effect of the Act or part`
#ASSERT `counts as a repeal or amendment for section 7` `the exclusion of the application of the Act or part to any person, subject-matter or circumstance`

§ `Sections 10, 10A, 11, 11B`

#ASSERT `a reference to the short title of another Act includes that Act as amended from time to time`
#ASSERT `the reference includes the re-enacted Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference includes the re-enacted Act` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the reference to the repealed provision extends to the re-enacted provision` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference to the repealed provision extends to the re-enacted provision` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference to the repealed provision extends to the re-enacted provision` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a reference to a citation of a law of a State or Territory includes that law as originally enacted or made and as amended from time to time`
#ASSERT `the reference includes the re-enacted or re-made law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference includes the re-enacted or re-made law` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the reference to the repealed provision of the State or Territory law extends to the re-enacted or re-made provision` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference to the repealed provision of the State or Territory law extends to the re-enacted or re-made provision` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `an Act may be altered, amended or repealed in the same session of Parliament in which it was passed`
#ASSERT `the term has that meaning in the non-amending provision` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the term has that meaning in the non-amending provision` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the term has that meaning in the non-amending provision` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the term has that meaning in the non-amending provision` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
